This is how long it took Team Fortress 2 to finally die. Though Valve did try their best to bring this game up to new game standards, they turned it into Counter-Strike: Global Offensive. Counter-Strike is a good game, but due to its toxic community and competitive nature I'm never actually able to have fun. The fact that Valve is bringing a more competitive vibe to Team Fortress 2 is very un-welcome to those who are non-competitive. It makes me sad to see such a great game die like the rest, but it had to happen one way or the other.
Because of these changes, I've decided to resign from Team Fortress 2 and turn in my badge as a mercenary for Mann Co. I realize I'm going to miss out on all the fun events (
), but with these current matchmaking settings and the way the matches turn out (
) are simply making the game less enjoyable to play. Regardless if Valve changes the matchmaking system to make the game more playable, my decision is final, and I will not be returning. If you like the new update, that's great! I hope you enjoy the
Team Fortress 2 experience. I on the other hand am cashing out to find a new game I can call home (
). However, I can say it has been a good run for the last four years I've played this game. So at least I can end it off on a good note.

